# Map-tile tooltip implementation checklist

## Goal

Extend DwarfUI's process-wide tooltip system so a feature can register an
exact fortress-map tile as a tooltip target. While a registration is eligible,
hovering the corresponding `{x, y, z}` tile must publish and render a normal
DwarfUI tooltip through the existing intent and presentation pipeline.

The first production consumer is the selected Minecart Route overlay. Its
same-z route-stop markers must expose map-tile tooltips without creating fake
widgets or adding minecart-specific behavior to the generic tooltip modules.

## Confirmed boundaries

- [ ] Use `dfhack.screen.getMousePos()` for the screen-cell tooltip anchor.
- [ ] Use `dfhack.gui.getMousePos()` for the map tile under the mouse.
- [ ] Copy the returned map coordinates into the immutable pointer sample; do
      not retain a mutable coordinate object across frames.
- [ ] Treat a missing or invalid map position as a map-target miss.
- [ ] Match map targets by exact integer `x`, `y`, and `z` equality.
- [ ] Keep `tooltip.register(widget)` and `tooltip.unregister(widget)`
      backward compatible.
- [ ] Keep the current process-wide invariant of at most one active tooltip
      target, intent, and rendered tooltip.
- [ ] Keep tooltip registration, sampling, hit detection, and intent mediation
      independent from rendering hosts.
- [ ] Continue presenting through the existing native-overlay or owning
      Lua-screen render seam selected from the intent's source root.
- [ ] Do not restore the retired `TooltipAgent` API.
- [ ] Do not construct a tooltip `gui.ZScreen`, `OverlayWidget`, focus owner,
      input recipient, or independent renderer.
- [ ] Do not manually reproduce DFHack's text-mode or Premium map projection.
- [ ] Do not add off-z, projected-column, rectangular-region, radius, or
      arbitrary-predicate hit modes.
- [ ] Do not make map-tile tooltips consume clicks or other native input.

## Public behavior contract

- [ ] Add `tooltip.register_map_tile(options)`, returning a stable registration
      handle.
- [ ] Add `tooltip.update_map_tile(handle, state)` for atomic position and
      text changes without replacing target identity.
- [ ] Add `tooltip.unregister_map_tile(handle)` for immediate idempotent
      removal.
- [ ] Require `options.owner` to identify the GUI view whose current root owns
      the target's eligibility, lifetime, and presentation transport.
- [ ] Require `options.pos` to contain integer `x`, `y`, and `z` fields and
      copy those values into registration-owned state.
- [ ] Accept tooltip text under the same string, empty-string, and `nil`
      semantics as widget tooltips.
- [ ] Retain weak cleanup as the safety net when a caller abandons a handle
      without explicit removal.
- [ ] Permit registration before owner attachment, but skip the target until
      the owner resolves to an eligible presented root.
- [ ] Make hidden, inactive, detached, disabled, stale, or viewscreen-mismatched
      owners ineligible.
- [ ] Permit multiple registrations at the same exact tile and resolve them
      with a documented deterministic registration order.
- [ ] Anchor the rendered tooltip to the sampled screen-cell pointer position,
      not to a separately projected tile position.
- [ ] Treat a registered widget target as higher precedence than a map-tile
      target.
- [ ] Prevent a map-tile tooltip from appearing through a DwarfUI widget or
      blocking region that owns the sampled screen cell.
- [ ] Permit pointer-transparent DwarfUI regions to fall through to an eligible
      map-tile target.

## Phase 0: Lock the generic contract and regression baseline

- [x] Add contract tests for the new public registration functions and handle
      behavior before integrating a production consumer.
- [x] Specify the registration handle's identity, update, removal, weak
      lifetime, and duplicate-tile behavior in LuaDoc.
- [x] Specify owner-to-root resolution independently from map hit testing.
- [x] Specify that exact map coordinates are hit data while the owner root is
      presentation and lifecycle data.
- [x] Specify that map registrations do not need, create, or imitate
      `gui.View` instances.
- [x] Record the current focused tooltip and minecart test baseline.
- [x] Preserve package-contract assertions that `TooltipAgent` is absent and
      tooltip input modules do not depend on presentation modules.
- [x] Add LuaDoc comments to every new or modified class and method.

### Phase 0 completion gate

- [x] The public API and lifecycle rules are represented by failing contract
      tests with no minecart-specific assumptions.
- [x] Existing widget registration behavior remains captured by its current
      unit and package-contract coverage.
- [x] The implementation boundary explicitly excludes off-z targets and manual
      screen-to-map projection.

## Phase 1: Extend immutable pointer sampling with map coordinates

- [x] Extend `dwarfui.PointerSample` with optional scalar `map_x`, `map_y`, and
      `map_z` fields while preserving existing screen `x` and `y` fields.
- [x] Read screen and map positions during the same scheduled pointer-poller
      callback.
- [x] Read `dfhack.gui.getMousePos()` only while the caller's
      live-map-registration demand predicate requires map sampling.
- [x] Preserve screen-only widget-tooltip behavior when no map registration
      exists.
- [x] Ensure every scheduled callback still emits at most one immutable sample
      with one monotonically increasing sequence number.
- [x] Preserve independent nil semantics: a screen anchor may exist while no
      valid map tile exists.
- [x] Add injected-sampler coverage for valid map coordinates, nil map
      coordinates, map-position changes, stopped demand, and module reload.
- [x] Add immutability coverage proving observers cannot mutate either
      coordinate space in a published sample.
- [x] Add regression coverage proving stale callbacks from an earlier poller
      generation cannot publish map samples.

### Phase 1 completion gate

- [x] One demanded poller callback produces a coherent screen/map snapshot
      without any map projection code in DwarfUI.
- [x] Widget-only registrations do not introduce unnecessary map sampling.
- [x] Nil map positions publish map-miss data without disturbing valid
      widget-targeting screen coordinates.

## Phase 2: Implement exact map-tile registration and detection

- [x] Add a presentation-independent map-tile registration module or class
      with caller-owned registration handles.
- [x] Keep live handles in weak registration state so the service does not
      retain abandoned consumers.
- [x] Maintain an exact-coordinate index instead of scanning every registered
      tile on every pointer sample.
- [x] Reindex a handle atomically when its position changes.
- [x] Remove empty coordinate buckets after updates, explicit removal, or weak
      cleanup.
- [x] Reuse one shared owner-root eligibility implementation for widget and
      map registrations instead of duplicating overlay, native-root, and
      Lua-screen rules.
- [x] Resolve only registrations whose owners currently map to an eligible
      presented root.
- [x] Return a presentation-neutral map-target candidate containing stable
      identity, source root, registration sequence, current text, and screen
      anchor data.
- [x] Resolve duplicate exact-tile registrations deterministically.
- [x] Add unit coverage for exact hits, x/y/z misses, nil map positions,
      duplicate tiles, position updates, removal, garbage collection,
      detachment, hidden/inactive owners, overlay disablement, wrong
      viewscreens, and reload.
- [x] Add regression coverage proving an equal `x,y` with a different `z`
      never hits.

### Phase 2 completion gate

- [x] Exact `{x, y, z}` lookup returns one deterministic eligible candidate or
      a miss.
- [x] Registration updates and cleanup leave no stale coordinate-index entry.
- [x] The map detector has no minecart, renderer, screen-host, or input
      dependency.

## Phase 3: Unify widget and map candidates in tooltip mediation

- [x] Introduce a normalized tooltip-target adapter understood by
      `TooltipService` without requiring every target to be a `gui.View`.
- [x] Give adapters stable target identity, current tooltip-text access,
      source-root access, and optional enter/update/leave transitions.
- [x] Adapt existing widget targets without changing their callback order,
      local coordinates, text validation, or weak registration semantics.
- [x] Adapt map registrations without adding widget-only fields or methods to
      their handles.
- [x] Build the screen-space root set from both widget registrations and
      map-registration owners.
- [x] Distinguish a genuine screen-space miss from a non-tooltip widget that
      nevertheless owns or blocks the pointer cell.
- [x] Select a registered widget tooltip before considering a map candidate.
- [x] Suppress map fallback for target-owned or blocked UI regions.
- [x] Allow map fallback only after pointer-transparent screen-space misses.
- [x] Publish the existing immutable tooltip intent shape with the sampled
      screen anchor and owning source root.
- [x] Leave `TooltipPresenter`, tooltip layout, and render-hook transport
      selection unchanged unless a failing contract demonstrates a required
      correction.
- [x] Count widget and map registrations together for poller demand while
      exposing separate counts in diagnostics.
- [x] Version process-owned service state deliberately and retire incompatible
      targets, intents, observers, and callbacks during reload.
- [x] Add service and registration coverage for widget-to-map, map-to-widget,
      map-to-map, blocked-to-map, map-to-miss, removal, and text-update
      transitions.
- [x] Add package-contract coverage proving the expanded input path remains
      independent from tooltip presentation modules.

### Phase 3 completion gate

- [x] Widgets and exact map tiles feed one ordered tooltip service without fake
      views or duplicate presenters.
- [x] UI controls and blockers cannot leak an underlying map tooltip.
- [x] Existing widget tooltip tests pass unchanged in behavior.
- [x] Map intents render through the existing owner-selected final render seam.

## Phase 4: Integrate same-z minecart route-stop markers

- [x] Keep all minecart-specific text, stop lookup, and selection rules in the
      minecart route overlay or its model.
- [x] Maintain map-tooltip registrations keyed by stable stop ID; do not retain
      native stop pointers across frames.
- [x] Derive each handle's current position and text from freshly resolved
      selected-route data.
- [x] Use the current custom stop name in the tooltip, with the existing
      unnamed-stop fallback.
- [x] Register or enable targets only for marker descriptors whose
      `marker_kind` is `same_z`.
- [x] Do not register a target for `above` or `below` marker descriptors.
- [x] Restrict the hit region to the marker's exact world tile; labels in
      adjacent screen cells are not map-tile targets.
- [x] Update registrations when stops are added, removed, renamed, moved, or
      reordered and when the selected route changes.
- [x] Clear minecart-owned registrations when selection clears, the route is
      deleted, the Hauling menu closes, the world unloads, the overlay is
      disabled, or the module reloads.
- [x] Preserve route-list click pass-through and all existing marker and label
      rendering.
- [x] Avoid world scans and inspect only the selected route and its stops.
- [x] Add focused overlay tests for same-z registration, exact position,
      current name, unnamed stops, position/name updates, duplicate stop
      positions, route changes, z-level changes, stale selection, and cleanup.
- [x] Add explicit regression coverage proving off-z markers never create or
      retain tooltip targets.

### Phase 4 completion gate

- [x] Hovering a same-z selected-route marker produces the current stop
      tooltip through the generic map-tile API.
- [x] Hovering an off-z marker produces no map-tile tooltip.
- [x] Minecart code contains no screen-to-map projection, tooltip renderer, or
      generic hit-system special case.
- [x] Selection, route editing, marker rendering, and native input behavior
      remain unchanged outside the new tooltip.

## Phase 5: Add native integration and complete validation

- [ ] Extend or add a DwarfSpec test whose filename ends only in `.ds.lua`.
- [ ] Mount the production Minecart Route overlay against the real native
      Hauling viewscreen and real `plotinfo.hauling` data.
- [ ] Move the physical test pointer over an actual rendered same-z marker
      before asserting hover behavior.
- [ ] Assert the sampled map position equals the native stop's exact
      `{x, y, z}` coordinates.
- [ ] Assert the final rendered tooltip contains the current native stop name,
      not duplicated fixture text.
- [ ] Move the pointer to the same `x,y` on a different z-level and verify the
      tooltip clears while the off-z marker remains non-interactive.
- [ ] Move the pointer over native or DwarfUI-owned UI covering the map and
      verify the map tooltip does not shine through.
- [ ] Rename or move only a disposable stop when mutation coverage is
      required, then verify the registration follows the fresh native data.
- [ ] Verify selection clear, Hauling-menu close, overlay disable, world
      unload, and `dwarfui reload` remove active map targets and rendered
      intent.
- [ ] Restore viewport, cursor, pointer position, selected route, overlay
      configuration, native route-menu state, and any disposable fixture even
      when an assertion fails.
- [ ] Require DwarfSpec to report `cleanup_confirmed=true` with no retained
      screen, subject, pointer patch, tooltip target, or changed game state.
- [ ] Run focused pointer, tooltip, map-target, minecart model, and minecart
      overlay unit tests.
- [ ] Run the focused DwarfSpec map-tooltip consumer test through
      `tools/Run-AutomationTests.ps1`.
- [ ] Run the complete standalone unit suite.
- [ ] Run the complete DwarfSpec suite through the same pass-through wrapper.
- [ ] Run Lua syntax validation for production, unit, support, and `.ds.lua`
      files.
- [ ] Run the offline build and verify expanded package contents.
- [ ] Run archive package verification.
- [ ] Run `git diff --check`.
- [ ] Install the packaged mod into the configured live DFHack instance and
      run `dwarfui reload`.
- [ ] Visually verify a same-z marker tooltip, the absence of off-z marker
      tooltips, UI occlusion, route switching, stop rename/move refresh, and
      cleanup.
- [ ] Review the DFHack console and logs for Lua errors after hover, movement,
      z-level changes, overlay disablement, and reload.
- [ ] Record focused, complete, syntax, package, cleanup, and live evidence
      separately.

### Phase 5 completion gate

- [ ] Focused and complete unit and DwarfSpec suites pass with zero failures.
- [ ] Syntax, offline build, expanded package, archive package, and diff checks
      pass.
- [ ] Native automation proves exact tile matching, final tooltip rendering,
      UI occlusion, same-z-only behavior, and confirmed cleanup.
- [ ] Live DFHack evidence confirms the packaged implementation without
      overstating unit, component, or offline-build coverage.

## Definition of done

- [ ] Any eligible DwarfUI owner can register an exact `{x, y, z}` map tile as
      a tooltip target through the public tooltip module.
- [ ] The pointer poller samples DFHack-provided map coordinates only while
      map-tooltip demand exists.
- [ ] Map-tile hit detection is indexed, deterministic, exact-z, and
      presentation independent.
- [ ] Widget targets and UI blockers take precedence over map-tile targets.
- [ ] Map registrations use their owner only for root eligibility, lifetime,
      and presentation transport.
- [ ] The existing intent, presenter, and final render seams display map
      tooltips without a new screen, overlay, renderer, or input owner.
- [ ] Same-z Minecart Route stop markers show current stop-name tooltips.
- [ ] Off-z Minecart Route markers never show or retain map-tile tooltips.
- [ ] Stop, route, owner, viewscreen, overlay, world, and reload lifecycle
      changes leave no stale registration or intent.
- [ ] Existing widget-tooltip behavior and native Minecart Route input/render
      behavior remain intact.
- [ ] All new and modified classes and methods have LuaDoc comments.
- [ ] Focused, complete, syntax, package, cleanup, and live verification
      evidence are recorded independently.

